From 67a38a7f039b6b0ebc8753eb851c1ce9f8017930 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DongDongJu <commisori28@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:52:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kv-events): replay native events after subscriber startup

A warm SGLang engine can publish retained CPU events before the native ZMQ
subscriber connects. Add optional replay to the existing listener and pass the
SGLang replay configuration through the Python wrapper. Preserve native medium,
identity, and ordering through the existing normalizer and event processor.

The opt-in nonce handshake proves that the live topic filter is installed before
replay begins. Pin the publisher incarnation, deduplicate replay/live sequences,
and repair detected gaps with bounded replay. Malformed or unavailable replay
terminates the configured source through existing supervisor cleanup. Ordinary
publishers keep their current transport and queue-admission behavior.

Validation: 104 Rust publisher tests, including real native socket replay and
source withdrawal after partial publication; 24 Dynamo SGLang Python tests;
Rustfmt, focused Clippy, and Python precommit checks. Clippy retains two existing
warnings in block-manager transfer validation. Live SGLang validation follows
with the matching native publisher handshake companion.

Co-authored-by: Dongjoo Seo <dongjoo.seo1@samsung.com>
Signed-off-by: DongDongJu <commisori28@gmail.com>
