+## Optional native replay
+
+`KvEventPublisher(zmq_replay_endpoint=...)` reads retained native engine batches
+before consuming the live SUB queue. It checks contiguous native sequence
+numbers and skips duplicate replay/live batches before normalization and outbound
+event-ID allocation. A detected live sequence gap requests the missing suffix
+from that same endpoint. Each replay request has a five-second deadline and a
+65,536-batch limit. A truncated prefix, unrepaired gap, malformed reply, or timeout
+stops the listener; its existing supervisor cancels the publisher and removes its
+source advertisement. Calls without a replay endpoint retain the existing live
+delivery behavior.
+
+`zmq_replay_handshake=True` additionally requires an engine supporting the nonce
+subscription challenge. The client sends a random, nonmatching topic over the
+replay DEALER, receives it back as a challenge, and subscribes to it on the same
+SUB socket after its native topic filter. The engine observes that subscription
+before serving replay, closing the empty-replay/live cutover race. Its challenge
+also supplies a 16-byte publisher incarnation; a change within one Dynamo source
+is terminal. The nonce is removed after replay or shutdown; it carries no KV
+event. Older engines remain compatible with the default, disabled handshake.
+
+Replay is bounded history, not a snapshot or a general lossless PUB transport.
+An undetectable final live-frame loss remains a transport limitation; this path
+does not add periodic polling, heartbeat events, or publication retries. Native
+publisher restart still requires a new Dynamo publisher identity as described
+by `KvEventPublisher`.
+
